Precompute FilmHost's per-channel curves once during DI setup.

Selective adaptation from JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab main at
d4b8145f6f9bdade15cda014776e99521adf0b5f, engine/src/core/digital_intermediate.cpp.
Source: https://github.com/JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab/blob/d4b8145f6f9bdade15cda014776e99521adf0b5f/engine/src/core/digital_intermediate.cpp

Copy the existing double samples once rather than allocating two temporary
vectors for every curve query. Keep the same interp function, query, knots,
sample order, DIR arithmetic, full colour fit and public DI signatures.
Do not import minilab or the log_positive_only early-return path.
Co-created with GPT (OpenAI), 2026-11-09.

